######################################################################
# Cursor Workspace Rules — UnitSchool Learning Platform
# Next.js 15 | React 19 | SCSS Modules | Tailwind CSS | i18n
######################################################################

## Core Principles
- Prioritize clarity and maintainability over cleverness
- Build small, focused, reusable components; avoid duplication
- Follow existing architecture and naming conventions
- Ship accessible, mobile-first, performant experiences by default
- Use latest stable best practices; remove deprecated patterns
- Always provide meaningful loading, empty, and error states
- ALWAYS use DRY code and best practices

## React & Next.js
- Use functional components with hooks
- Follow App Router conventions in `src/app/**`
- Write new components in JavaScript (unless directory uses TypeScript)
- Co-locate component-specific styles using SCSS modules
- Add error boundaries where failure isolation is meaningful
- Use `react-icons` for all icons
- Prefer modular utilities in `src/utils/**`

## Styling (SCSS)
- Use SCSS modules and variables from `src/assets/styles/_settings.scss`
- Use design tokens for colors/spacing; use `$error-color` (not `$danger-color`)
- Modern Sass only:
  - Import with `@use`/`@forward` (no `@import`)
  - Use `sass:color` module (e.g., `color.adjust($c, $lightness: 10%)`)
  - Use `sass:math` module (e.g., `math.div()` for division)
- **Mixin positioning**: Place `@include mixin-name` AFTER other properties and BEFORE nested selectors
  - ✅ `color: $primary; padding: 1rem; @include flex(); .nested {}`
  - ❌ `@include flex(); color: $primary;` or `color: $primary; .nested {} @include flex();`
- Avoid mixed declarations: don't place declarations after nested rules
- Mobile-first responsiveness: cover all relevant breakpoints
- Prefer WebP/AVIF with appropriate fallbacks

## Internationalization (i18n)
- Translations in `src/locales/{en,ru,uz}/` with consistent files across languages
- Always pass correct namespace to `useTranslation('namespace')`
- Reuse existing translation keys; add new keys to all supported languages
- Design UI for text expansion and RTL when relevant

## Accessibility & UX
- Comply with WCAG 2.1 AA where feasible
- Ensure keyboard navigation and visible focus states
- Provide descriptive labels, roles, and alt text
- Maintain logical heading order and landmark regions
- Ensure adequate contrast ratios; respect reduced motion preferences
- iOS compatibility: 375px–428px widths, 44x44px touch targets, safe areas

## Performance & Assets
- Lazy-load non-critical components and assets
- Use code-splitting; avoid shipping unused dependencies
- Ensure CLS-safe image dimensions and stable layout
- Prefer modern image formats (WebP/AVIF) with fallbacks

## State Management
- Centralize cross-cutting state in `src/store/**`
- Keep local UI state within components/hooks
- Memoize expensive computations and heavy lists
- Handle empty, loading, and error states consistently

## Documentation & Delivery
- NEVER create markdown (.md) files unless explicitly requested
- After completing tasks, provide concise, actionable suggestions for improvement
- Keep summaries and explanations in chat interface only

## Ignore
.next/**, node_modules/**, .git/**, src/store/data.json

######################################################################
USE ONLY BEST PRACTICES AND MOST RECENT TECHNOLOGIES
######################################################################
